Vita: --vita-fast-pad=off|on|verify (platform/vita/runtime/fast_actors.hpp switch 9). The console
session of 10 Nov measured the tick input step at 1.50 ms per game tick in every place; in Vita3K 94 % of
it is PADRead, which asks SDL for about forty gamepad buttons and axes per tick, one locked call
each. SDL's gamepad state changes only while SDL pumps events (window::poll_events, on the thread
that reads the pads), so the fast path keeps the values asked since the last pump: each button or
axis is asked at most once per pump, a second game tick of the frame asks nothing, and a button
the pad's SDL mapping does not have reads up without a call. The PADStatus is the same bit for bit.
Verify asks SDL every time as before, uses its answer and counts the reads whose kept value
differed. Off (the default without the platform hook) is the unchanged code path.

--vita-fast-pad-events=off|on|verify (switch 10, with --vita-fast-pad on; console, 10 Nov left PADRead at
0.98 ms per frame, about 25 SDL calls): the kept values are no longer dropped at every pump but
brought up to date by SDL's own gamepad button and axis events, which window::process_event hands
to the pad code before any PADRead; SDL is asked only for a value not seen since the pad was added
or remapped. Verify asks SDL every time, uses its answer and counts the reads whose kept value
differed.

